! -------------------------------------------------------------------- !
! ww3-lab example 02 : convert GFS netCDF winds -> wind.ww3
!
! Run as:   ww3_prnc          (it reads ww3_prnc.nml, so symlink/copy this)
!
! ww3_prnc interpolates a forcing field from its own netCDF grid onto the
! model grid and writes WW3's internal binary format. One invocation per
! forcing type; you rename the namelist between runs.
!
! The input file is what get_gfs.sh writes: GFS 0.25 deg UGRD/VGRD at 10 m,
! subset to the box, merged along time and converted with ecCodes'
! grib_to_netcdf. That converter names the two fields by their ecCodes
! shortName with the digits moved last -- 10u/10v become u10/v10 -- and the
! coordinates longitude / latitude / time.
! -------------------------------------------------------------------- !

&FORCING_NML
  FORCING%FIELD%WINDS     = T
  FORCING%GRID%LATLON     = T
  FORCING%TIMESTART       = '20240701 000000'
  FORCING%TIMESTOP        = '20240708 000000'
/

&FILE_NML
  FILE%FILENAME  = 'gfs_winds.nc'
  FILE%LONGITUDE = 'longitude'
  FILE%LATITUDE  = 'latitude'
  FILE%VAR(1)    = 'u10'
  FILE%VAR(2)    = 'v10'
/

! ⚠ Verify the variable and coordinate names against your actual file:
!     ncdump -h gfs_winds.nc | head -40
! and adjust FILE%VAR / FILE%LONGITUDE / FILE%LATITUDE if they differ (an
! older or newer ecCodes may emit 'u10'/'v10' as '10u'/'10v', or a 'step'
! axis next to 'time' if the conversion did not fold it into valid time).
!
! ⚠ Also check the longitude convention. GFS is on 0..360; get_gfs.sh
! relabels to -180..180 so it overlaps our -52..-44 grid. If they disagree,
! ww3_prnc will either error or -- worse -- silently give you a field of
! zeros. Fix by hand with:
!     ncap2 -O -s 'where(longitude > 180.0) longitude = longitude - 360.0;' gfs_winds.nc gfs_winds.nc
!
! ⚠ FORCING%TIMESTART/TIMESTOP must lie inside the file's time axis; retime
! them (and the other three dated namelists) to the cycle you fetched --
! get_gfs.sh prints the sed to do it.
! -------------------------------------------------------------------- !
